<?php
/**
 * Hub Market override of Mageplaza_LayeredNavigation's filter template.
 *
 * THE CHECKBOX IN FRONT OF EVERY FILTER OPTION IS DECORATION.
 *
 * It carries no name, no id, no value and no handler — the <a> beside it is the
 * control that actually applies the filter, and it already carries the option
 * label and the count as its accessible name. The input exists so the option
 * LOOKS like a checkbox.
 *
 * Left as-is it is a focusable form control with no accessible name at all. That
 * was invisible while the rail shipped collapsed; opening the filters to match
 * the design (see _hm-figma.less) put fifteen of them on the category page, and
 * the site sweep caught the jump from 4 unnamed controls to 19.
 *
 * aria-hidden + tabindex="-1" rather than a label: giving it a name would put a
 * SECOND tab stop on every option that does nothing when activated, which is
 * worse for keyboard users than the visual-only element it actually is.
 *
 * Only those two attributes are added. Everything else is Mageplaza's.
 */
?>
<?php
